        "id": 158544,
        "name": "danmarshall14",
        "username": "danmarshall14",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/danmarshall14/{size}/1944_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-02-21T13:13:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Donner\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/donner/48/1903_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Donner:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Ouch.  Anyone who has to cheat to win isn’t really winning.  They’re admitting they can’t win by playing by the rules.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>People do strange things when they get competitive and tournaments can bring out the worst in them. I mostly prefer coop games for this reason.  But Netrunner is just a fantastic game and the community is overall full of helpful,  kind players.  Every now and again though you run into folks that are clearly on the warpath to win.</p>",
